1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,600
BOYS'
BASKETBALL
TEAM

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:04,600
Wrong... correct... wrong...

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,080
ANSWER

4
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:07,080
And wrong.

5
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:10,040
I've finished grading all of the tests.

6
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:12,080
And the results?

7
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:15,210
It's unfortunate, but...

8
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:18,670
Every single one of you...

9
00:00:19,210 --> 00:00:20,630
...actually got a passing grade!

10
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:23,080
What the hell is "unfortunate" about that?!

11
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:27,040
Oops, sorry about that. What I meant to say was,
"It's my pleasure to announce!"

12
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:33,470
That being said, please don't get too relaxed
about the midterms.

13
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:36,000
All I did was check them to give us an idea.

14
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:38,500
My grading might be 2 or 3 points off
from the actual results.

15
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:40,680
That's hardly gonna make any difference.

16
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,290
It will because you guys are 
just barely passing as it is!

17
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:47,150
Well... I'll acknowledge that 
they've put in the effort.

18
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:51,290
After all, this lot has only managed
single-digit grades up until now.

19
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:55,130
With all their progress recently,
it would be nice to see a win tomorrow.

20
00:00:57,710 --> 00:00:59,540
Of course! We've totally got this in the bag!

21
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,250
Everybody here is in it to win it.

22
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,380
I hope our reward is sushi this time.

23
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,380
Sushi, hell yeah!

24
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,460
Quit begging for a free 
meal after every damn game!

25
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:12,920
All right! This is our last practice sesh!
Let's throw everything we've got into it!

26
00:01:13,290 --> 00:01:14,540
Right!

27
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:45,960
Ahiru no Sora

28
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:49,500
Undiscovered Talent

29
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:48,000
Did you see the tourney bracket?

30
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,500
Our first opponent is gonna be Kuzu High!

31
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:52,130
What? Does Kuzu High even 
have a basketball team?

32
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,830
They're new this year, aren't they?

33
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,540
Ugh. Isn't that the school with 
a team full of delinquents?

34
00:02:56,790 --> 00:02:59,960
Well, at least we know they 
probably suck at the game.

35
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:03,290
Guess that means we're gonna
glide through the first round!

36
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:05,830
The big problem for us are the teams who come after.

37
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:07,740
Both Saijo and Shinmaruko are in our bracket, right?

38
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:10,910
Oh yeah, isn't Shinmaruko the team
from the Kanto tourney that- Ow!

39
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:13,790
It's impossible to know
the outcome of a match beforehand.

40
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:16,880
Quit belittling our opponents 
before we even play them.

41
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:19,130
Oh. Sorry, Captain Takahashi!

42
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:20,340
W-we won't do it again!

43
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:23,800
Required Training For All
Running - 5 Minutes
Stretching
Slides - Full Court 5 Times
Squats - Full Court 5 Times
Sprints - x 100
No Slacking

44
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,290
Have you done your warmups?

45
00:03:22,290 --> 00:03:23,800
N-not yet!

46
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,290
Get them done fast.

47
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:28,130
Huh? Senpai, isn't that popsicle...?

48
00:03:28,130 --> 00:03:30,580
This? I found it in the freezer.

49
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,580
Because it's mine, I put it there!

50
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,420
Oh, my bad. I'll pay you back 50 yen later.

51
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:37,000
But it cost me 100 yen!

52
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:39,670
There he goes again.

53
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,110
Just when I think he's doing a solid job as leader,

54
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:43,950
he goes and acts all aloof like that.

55
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:46,040
Doesn't even look nervous.

56
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,750
But that's a good thing.

57
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:50,080
It's part of what makes 
our Captain who he is.

58
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:51,460
'Sup?!

59
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,330
Good arf-ternoon, dawgs.

60
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:57,880
Hey, Kojima!

61
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,460
Is your leg injury doing better now?

62
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:00,630
It's doing just purr-fect.

63
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:04,090
Don't bother trying to fool us,
we know that you tore a ligament.

64
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:08,750
If I miss out on this tournament,
then my High School basketball career is over.

65
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:11,080
I don't want to have any regrets.

66
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,080
Noooo!

67
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:18,540
You're on the bench for now.

68
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:23,250
But no need to worry,
I'll get us through at least the first 3 games.

69
00:04:23,710 --> 00:04:26,290
What a wimp! Can't even go all the way!

70
00:04:26,290 --> 00:04:27,950
Oh yeah?! Take this!

71
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:29,670
Hey, did you know?

72
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,800
When Takahashi and Kojima joined
the basketball team here,

73
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:35,180
they were the only 2 members.

74
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:35,880
Huh?!

75
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:39,580
They spent every day
of their freshman year playing 1-on-1.

76
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:43,080
Then in their sophomore year, 
some others finally joined,

77
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:45,000
but that only brought them up to 5 members.

78
00:04:45,130 --> 00:04:47,040
So apparently they lost 
every match they played.

79
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:51,830
Seriously? That's crazy, considering how awesome
Takahashi is on the court...

80
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:55,080
Well, you gotta remember we're in
the same region as Saijo and Kitasumi.

81
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,580
Ever since we joined the team this year,

82
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,480
it was like everything had finally come together,

83
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:03,130
but then in our last game,
Kojima ended up injuring his leg...

84
00:05:05,790 --> 00:05:07,040
Hey, you freshmen.

85
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:08,540
Uh, yessir!

86
00:05:08,790 --> 00:05:10,710
Who was in charge of mopping the court today?

87
00:05:10,790 --> 00:05:12,250
Th-that would be us, sir!

88
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:14,750
Do it again!

89
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:18,330
Man, Kashiwagi really terrifies me!

90
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:21,300
Yeah, he's seriously the only 
senior I just can't deal with!

91
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:25,170
I don't think I've ever seen him
actually mop the court even once!

92
00:05:25,330 --> 00:05:28,330
But Takashi and the other 
seniors do it all the time!

93
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,500
Just imagine this team if he wasn't around...

94
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,080
Shut up! He'll hear you!

95
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:35,630
We're starting! Hurry it up!

96
00:05:35,630 --> 00:05:36,630
Yessir!

97
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:39,330
Freshmen! I expect louder cheering today.

98
00:05:39,330 --> 00:05:39,960
Yessir!

99
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:42,040
Tanaka, get your foot off the line.

100
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:44,630
Shinjo...!

101
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,000
FIGHT!

102
00:06:02,290 --> 00:06:04,340
Uh, hello? Nanao?

103
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:07,540
I just wanted to confirm 
some details about tomorrow.

104
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:10,040
First, could you tell me what 
I need to bring with me?

105
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:14,790
Right, okay. So then, 
you'll bring our uniforms.

106
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:17,920
Yep. I think you've got all you need.

107
00:06:18,130 --> 00:06:21,130
You're more of a worrywart
than I would have expected, Kurumatani.

108
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:24,750
Uh, yeah. It's cuz I somehow
always manage to forget stuff.

109
00:06:25,170 --> 00:06:27,790
Tomorrow is finally the 
big day. Are you nervous?

110
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:30,210
Huh? No! Not at all!

111
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:32,630
Make sure you go to bed
as early as possible tonight, okay?

112
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:33,420
Right.

113
00:06:33,630 --> 00:06:35,920
Uh, so we're meeting at 
8:00 am tomorrow, right?

114
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,540
I just told you that a minute ago.

115
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,250
Let's give it our all.

116
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:42,460
Yeah.

117
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:45,710
Okay, goodnight.

118
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,720
Yeah, nighty night.

119
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:01,100
I better check just one more time!

120
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:04,380
Hello? Kite?

121
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:06,420
I just wanna confirm about tomorrow...

122
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,380
Why are you calling THIS late, dumbass?!

123
00:07:12,710 --> 00:07:14,630
I thought your game didn't start 'til noon.

124
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:16,380
Aren't you leaving just a tad too early?

125
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:19,290
I'm leaving early so I can go to school
and get some practice in.

126
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:22,630
You'll wear yourself out
before the game even starts, then!

127
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:24,250
It'll be okay!

128
00:07:24,670 --> 00:07:25,790
I'm off!

129
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:30,330
I tried, but I couldn't sleep a wink!

130
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:33,140
This is the first time in my life...

131
00:07:33,710 --> 00:07:35,290
...that I've ever been so hyped up!

132
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,330
The sun is so bright this morning.

133
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,750
How beautiful...

134
00:08:03,790 --> 00:08:05,750
That... threw me for a loop!

135
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:13,210
That's right, today is...

136
00:08:14,670 --> 00:08:18,350
You've really grown so much
in the time I haven't seen you.

137
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:22,130
Do your best out there... Sora!

138
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,210
What the-?

139
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:30,210
Oh... hey, Tinytown.

140
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:32,420
What are all of you guys doing here?!

141
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:35,170
Don't tell me that you never 
actually left yesterday...

142
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:40,290
Nah, we went home for a bit,
but... we just couldn't sleep at all.

143
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:43,860
So we decided to try and do some extra practice on our shots...

144
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:46,420
but then all of a sudden it was morning.

145
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,500
I'm dead tired...

146
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,000
Yeah, you said it...

147
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,670
The world is turning white...

148
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,750
This is an absolute disaster!

149
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:58,330
You see? I told you they'd be here.

150
00:08:58,710 --> 00:08:59,600
I don't believe this.

151
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:03,100
Chiaki?! Did something happen to you?!
It's 6:00 in the morning!

152
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:06,330
When it comes to trips or events,
I'm always up bright and early.

153
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:08,790
Don't tell me that both of you also...

154
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:11,000
We were up playing games all night.

155
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:13,710
That means our team is in the 
worst condition right now!

156
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:17,750
You can go in before me, beanstalk.

157
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:18,670
Huh?

158
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:21,150
I don't want them thinking we're all buddy-buddy by

159
00:09:21,150 --> 00:09:22,440
showing up at the exact same time.

160
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:25,170
Thanks. Good to know you care so much.

161
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:25,880
Wha-?

162
00:09:31,130 --> 00:09:32,580
Ouch...

163
00:09:33,290 --> 00:09:35,170
I... I'm so sorry...

164
00:09:35,170 --> 00:09:36,310
You brainless moron!

165
00:09:36,310 --> 00:09:38,660
We'd be screwed if you went and injured me right before our match!

166
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,790
I kinda wish she had.

167
00:09:45,630 --> 00:09:47,460
Just you wait, Mom.

168
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,630
I'm definitely coming to see you soon!

169
00:10:02,830 --> 00:10:04,330
FIGHT WITH
ALL YOUR MIGHT

170
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:14,250
Whoa, teams are already practicing.

171
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:16,550
Must be the ones competing first today.

172
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:19,470
Ow! Watch it, punk!

173
00:10:19,470 --> 00:10:21,330
Oh... sorry about that.

174
00:10:20,170 --> 00:10:21,930
NAKANE

175
00:10:22,170 --> 00:10:25,000
Well, those guys are clearly 
good at basketball...

176
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:28,890
Yeah and based just on looks,
we're leaving the exact opposite impression...

177
00:10:39,130 --> 00:10:41,420
Yahoo!

178
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:43,750
WHAT THE HELL DO YOU THINK YOU'RE DOING?!

179
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:45,660
I, uh, I'm really sorry!

180
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:48,420
I honestly dunno what's 
gotten into me right now.

181
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,630
Yeah, man. I feel ya.

182
00:10:52,170 --> 00:10:53,830
What's wrong with you, Mokichi?

183
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:56,210
It's my anemia... I'm gonna pass out...

184
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,750
Then go home, stupid!

185
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,680
You guys are as lively as ever.

186
00:11:02,130 --> 00:11:02,920
Yo.

187
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:05,960
Hey, it's Tokiwa! And the 
other guys from Maru High!

188
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,790
Sheesh, the first round of a tournament
isn't anything to jump for joy over.

189
00:11:10,790 --> 00:11:12,750
Just watching you is 
already making me cringe.

190
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,880
Win 2 and you get to play us.

191
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,690
We're expecting to see you there.

192
00:11:17,790 --> 00:11:18,650
Count on it!

193
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,750
That reminds me, Chiba.
How are you guys fairing in the Kanto Tournament?

194
00:11:23,170 --> 00:11:25,880
If I remember right, it's held alongside
the inter-high prelims, yeah?

195
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:28,960
That's right. We just played 
a game earlier this week.

196
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,290
But we lost in the quarterfinals.

197
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:37,790
It's unbelievable, we can't even get ourselves
in the top 5. Just pathetic.

198
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:41,330
Except, the opposing team was
a well-known inter-high favorite.

199
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:42,970
I'd say we just had bad luck.

200
00:11:43,290 --> 00:11:45,630
That doesn't make them unbeatable.

201
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:47,680
We'll get our revenge the next time around.

202
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:50,570
We're scheduled to play the very last game today,

203
00:11:50,570 --> 00:11:52,650
so we'll be having fun watching your match in the meantime.

204
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,290
Shoo! Git!

205
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:56,920
So even Maru High couldn't 
be the prefectural reps.

206
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,830
We've got a long road to the top.

207
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,130
Those guys are just small 
fries, if you ask me.

208
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:06,290
Long time no see... my friends.

209
00:12:07,790 --> 00:12:09,290
Oh, it's just Farto Kabachi.

210
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:11,250
My name is TARO Kabachi!

211
00:12:11,630 --> 00:12:13,000
C'mon, let's get warmed up.

212
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,750
Hey! Don't just ignore me!

213
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:18,920
Actually, thinking about it,
Kitasumi isn't even playing here...

214
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:19,710
Huh?

215
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,830
Yeah, well, you see...

216
00:12:22,170 --> 00:12:24,680
I wanted to come and make sure
that Nao didn't forget about me.

217
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,630
So, you're gonna die soon?

218
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:27,630
Bye-bye.

219
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:29,250
Nobody is dying, dammit!

220
00:12:30,830 --> 00:12:33,540
Our game is getting ready to start!
Where the hell are you?!

221
00:12:34,830 --> 00:12:37,250
I'm gonna make you guys 
regret this! Stupid jerks!

222
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:46,540
From what I hear, Kuzu High
just barely formed their basketball team.

223
00:12:46,630 --> 00:12:50,500
According to our coach, a number
of their players are complete amateurs.

224
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,540
I kinda feel an affinity 
for them, knowing that.

225
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:56,830
It's starting to push my excitement level
through the woof!

226
00:12:57,330 --> 00:12:59,290
Well, since we're both bottom 
tier teams I hope this'll be-

227
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:01,050
Don't be stupid, we're more experienced.

228
00:13:02,830 --> 00:13:06,380
We kept pushing for those 3 years,
just so that we could get to this tournament.

229
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:09,470
Bottom tier or not, anybody playing high school

230
00:13:09,470 --> 00:13:11,890
basketball has dreams of going to the inter-high.

231
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:17,790
And I...

232
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,670
...want to blaze a trail for this team.

233
00:13:25,130 --> 00:13:26,880
Don't start laughing at me, freshmen.

234
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:28,790
W-we would never think of it!

235
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:31,830
I have dreams just like you said!
Please take us to the inter-high!

236
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:33,500
We're counting on you!

237
00:13:35,710 --> 00:13:36,750
You guys...

238
00:13:38,710 --> 00:13:42,750
Don't phrase it like that, be more positive and say,
"Let's all get there together."

239
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:44,960
You guys are gonna be playing out there, too.

240
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:46,960
We've got high hopes for all of you.

241
00:13:47,170 --> 00:13:48,430
Y-yessir!

242
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,920
Okay! Let's do this!

243
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,720
Everything starts by winning the first game.

244
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:57,060
Don't let your guard down just because they seem weak!

245
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,500
Let's get out there and win this thing!

246
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:02,040
Yeah!

247
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:05,460
KUZURYU

248
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:12,250
I'm so glad I made it back in time.

249
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,390
I can't believe I forgot the jerseys after I

250
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:16,120
brought them all the way to school this morning!

251
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:17,880
These are sick!

252
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,580
You've got it on backwards, dummy!

253
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:22,460
And these are your new 
t-shirts for practice, look!

254
00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:25,670
Momoharu even came up
with a really cool design for the backside!

255
00:14:25,790 --> 00:14:28,420
Don't you guys think they 
all turned out really good?

256
00:14:30,050 --> 00:14:34,540
DRAGON BALL

257
00:14:30,290 --> 00:14:34,210
Oh, it says "Ryu Kyu." I get it.
You took the "Ryu" from Kuzuryu.

258
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:37,330
Huh? You've got it totally wrong, you idiot.

259
00:14:37,330 --> 00:14:40,000
This is what "basket ball" looks like
when you write it with proper kanji.

260
00:14:41,940 --> 00:14:44,790
I think the word you actually 
wanted was "Rou Kyu."

261
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:46,920
BASKET BALL

262
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:46,920
That's the kanji for basket 
that I remember... yeah.

263
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:49,380
DRAGON BALL

264
00:14:49,630 --> 00:14:52,250
That's fine! It's all 
good if we understand it!

265
00:14:52,250 --> 00:14:55,460
Everyone will figure out that it's meant to be
the Ryu from Kuzuryu!

266
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:00,000
That's the end of the 2nd quarter!

267
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:01,630
Sweet, let's get moving!

268
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:06,460
The teams playing in the next game
get to practice on the court during halftime.

269
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:08,420
Shinjo...!

270
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:11,330
Fight! Yeah!

271
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,830
Wow... those guys are really pumped up.

272
00:15:18,330 --> 00:15:20,790
Any team giving off energy like that
has got to be tough to beat...

273
00:15:21,830 --> 00:15:24,790
We sure as hell aren't gonna win
if you let them psych you out now.

274
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:27,250
I know you guys have more guts than that.

275
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:29,790
He's right.

276
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:32,420
A'ight, boys! Time for us to get out there
and make some noise!

277
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:34,250
Raise the roof!

278
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:40,830
Did the lead up time to a match
always make me this nervous?

279
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:43,540
Dammit! I'm a real sad sack of shit.

280
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:49,210
What's up with that tiny kid?

281
00:15:49,210 --> 00:15:51,010
Did they accidentally let an 
elementary schooler in here?

282
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:55,210
There's no way that kid even 
reaches 160 centimeters.

283
00:15:55,290 --> 00:15:56,680
Totally, he's gotta be a sub or something.

284
00:15:58,830 --> 00:16:02,140
Though... is it just me
or has he not missed a single shot?

285
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:03,630
What's going on?

286
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,460
They're saying there's an 
amazing shooter down there.

287
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,130
Oh sweet, Shinjo's playing next!

288
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:09,040
They've got some solid players on their team.

289
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:11,210
An afro and a pompadour?

290
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:13,380
What's up with that team of weirdos?

291
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,290
Looks like it'll be an entertaining matchup.

292
00:16:15,290 --> 00:16:16,660
Let's go check it out for a bit!

293
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:18,040
Dammit...

294
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,620
You better not be thinking 
about playing today.

295
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:25,110
Give me a break.

296
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:27,890
You don't have to harp on me
every chance you get, dude!

297
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:29,740
I get it! Order received, Captain!

298
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:31,940
I'm just gonna
sit here and watch quietly from the bench!

299
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:33,190
Okay! Fine!

300
00:16:34,130 --> 00:16:35,050
But one condition...

301
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,010
I get to beat the shit 
outta you if we lose this.

302
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:41,480
Sure. Feel free.

303
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,460
That's the end of the game!

304
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:46,710
Alright!

305
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:53,210
Okay so, Chiaki, Kurumatani,
Natsume, Yasuhara, and Momoharu.

306
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,920
The five of you will be our starting lineup.

307
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:58,380
We're not going to be sloppy
and wait it out like we did before.

308
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:01,080
We're putting our best foot 
forward right from the start.

309
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:04,330
Chiaki, I want you to be as aggressive as possible
by getting under the basket.

310
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:07,960
If the flow of the game dictates it,
feel free to change positions with Kurumatani.

311
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,090
Sure, leave it to me.

312
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:12,210
This is our first battle. Let's 
tear it up out there, Yasuhara.

313
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:13,550
You got it!

314
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,580
Attention. The second match on court A,

315
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:22,750
Kuzuryu High School vs. Shinjotowa Academy
will now begin.

316
00:17:34,710 --> 00:17:49,500
SHI-N-JO! SHI-N-JO! SHI-N-JO! SHI-N-JO!

317
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,420
It's all you, Yukio.

318
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:40,420
Okay.

319
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:46,830
This guy is like a damn skyscraper!

320
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,500
Why are all the guys I 
go up against so huge?!

321
00:17:50,830 --> 00:17:53,710
Well, this guy isn't that 
imposing compared to Chiba.

322
00:17:53,710 --> 00:17:56,840
A difference of 7 or 8 centimeters
sure as hell ain't gonna stop me!

323
00:17:58,040 --> 00:17:59,630
I gotta get my nerves under control!

324
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:04,960
This a tournament, which means we're out
if we lose even once!

325
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:09,460
Yo, Yasuhara! You're facing the wrong way!

326
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,630
This is bad. Everyone's a nervous wreck!

327
00:18:12,630 --> 00:18:15,920
I bet scoring the first basket 
would snap them out of it.

328
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:20,130
But I can't expect that to happen
with our Captain like that.

329
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:23,370
It's a damn shame, since they're all usually
really smooth on the court.

330
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:30,330
Shit! I screwed up the timing!

331
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:34,580
Pass it here!

332
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:36,540
C'mon! Let's make this first one count!

333
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:38,430
We're playing man-to-man defense!

334
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:41,390
Get moving, Yasuhara! Don't 
forget who you're guarding!

335
00:18:41,710 --> 00:18:42,850
It's #7!

336
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,670
Don't get yourself in a panic, Yanagihara.

337
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:48,830
Just do it like we practiced.

338
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:52,210
I've taken the court during 
plenty of games, so I'm okay!

339
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,790
Please rest assured and let 
me take over for Kojima!

340
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:59,580
Remind me, aren't you friends
with that #4 down there, Chiba?

341
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,830
Yep. We were on the same
junior basketball team together.

342
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:05,500
Back then, we both got 
assigned to be point guard.

343
00:19:05,830 --> 00:19:09,710
It's because of Takahashi
that I hardly ever got put in a real game.

344
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,080
Oh?

345
00:19:11,330 --> 00:19:13,170
Make sure you watch closely, Tokiwa.

346
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:17,000
There's more undiscovered talent in this world
than you can shake a stick at.

347
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:20,630
Not every player out there is 
just plain lucky like we are.

348
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:24,580
He got by!

349
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:27,020
So fast... despite being so tall?!

350
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:29,500
Dammit! His good looks pissed 
me off enough already!

351
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:31,940
Right down the middle! He's like a flash!

352
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:34,900
He's just trying to pull defenders off
and pass to the big guy!

353
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:36,130
It's so obvious!

354
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:37,820
Right on the mark!

355
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:40,580
Nice! It's all mine! It'll be a turnover!

356
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,920
He stopped?! In the middle of it?!

357
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:48,500
Screen!

358
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,370
Switch, Yasu!

359
00:19:54,170 --> 00:19:55,130
The first basket!

360
00:19:55,130 --> 00:19:56,300
They're so awesome!

361
00:19:56,670 --> 00:19:57,710
That was smooth...

362
00:19:57,710 --> 00:20:00,260
I'm starting to think this 
team might be really good...

363
00:20:00,670 --> 00:20:01,880
Amazing.

364
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:04,670
They were all so calm and 
recovered really fast.

365
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,720
This is a team that's really in control!

366
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:08,670
Hey, bro.

367
00:20:09,670 --> 00:20:11,080
Nice job, Yanagihara!

368
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,900
All right! Let's keep this up!

369
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:29,290
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense!

370
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,170
What is happening?

371
00:20:16,630 --> 00:20:19,210
We just barely started... 
but I can hardly breathe...

372
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:21,400
That doesn't look good.

373
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:23,130
They got overwhelmed.

374
00:20:23,130 --> 00:20:24,880
The other team will run away with it.

375
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:27,080
Okay, time for defense!

376
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:27,830
Right!

377
00:20:28,330 --> 00:20:29,290
We'll shut them dow-

378
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,710
What the-? Was that a gust of wind?

379
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,330
Hey, Ref.

380
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:52,580
He hit me just now.

381
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:56,750
Th-the basket counts! One free-throw!

382
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,960
Huh? What just happened?

383
00:20:59,250 --> 00:21:01,190
He took it all the way alone.

384
00:21:01,750 --> 00:21:03,920
Well damn, this is a shocker.

385
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:08,250
Another trove of undiscovered talent...

386
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:13,170
...was waiting to be found 
right there, of all places.

387
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:17,500
That... was totally nuts.

388
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:19,340
I'm so glad he's on OUR team...

389
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:23,500
I've seen any number of players
who could be considered good...

390
00:21:24,290 --> 00:21:26,960
But... this guy is...

391
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:29,260
...way beyond even that level.

392
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:32,330
I'll give you two minutes.

393
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:36,170
Take that time to shake off your nerves.

394
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,960
You better start getting used to this,
or you'll waste precious stamina.

395
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:41,830
That's Kite for you.

396
00:21:41,830 --> 00:21:44,290
He's always there to step up 
at the most crucial times.

397
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:45,710
It's incredible.

398
00:21:46,170 --> 00:21:49,580
Smug jackass. But damn if he ain't reliable!

399
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:52,130
Hey. I'm totally fine, just so you know.

400
00:21:52,830 --> 00:21:54,540
I wasn't talking about you, bro.

401
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:56,500
Here they come!

402
00:21:56,790 --> 00:21:58,960
A'ight! We're on defense!

403
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,250
Let's stop 'em cold!

404
00:23:30,970 --> 00:23:35,390
Ahiru no Sora

405
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:34,420
Next time: "Rush and Rush."

